MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The WYZE Cam v3 feels like a useful next choice because I have bought security cameras before, and its color night vision and two-way audio give me specific reasons to consider it for another monitoring spot.",
    "The Echo Show 8 fits my interest in connected home devices while adding a screen for video calls, giving me a new use alongside my Fire TV equipment."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "More Fire TV streaming devices mostly repeat what my existing 4K stick and Fire TV television already do; the HD stick is especially unappealing because it offers less than my current setup.",
    "Echo Auto and AirPods Pro address car assistance and personal listening, neither of which is a need I have right now. Sharing a broad connection to electronics does not make them useful next purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest several more streaming devices, even though those purchases already cover my viewing needs.",
    "Alexa compatibility seems to carry too much weight by itself. A smart plug or voice-only speaker still needs a specific purpose in my home before I would choose it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about what a device adds to equipment I already own: another monitoring location or video calling is more compelling than another way to stream to a television.",
    "Specific capabilities affect my choice between similar products. The v3's advertised color night vision makes it more appealing than the v2, while a screen makes the Echo Show more useful to me this time than an Echo Dot."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions understand my interest in home viewing and monitoring, but too often treat familiar devices and Alexa compatibility as reasons to buy without identifying a new use."
}
